    "scientific_verdict": "Across k in {2, 3} oracle calls and secret subspaces W_S subseteq F_q^n, averaging over s ~ Unif(W_S) pinches the trajectory sum onto V_epsilon(f; W_S) = {(w, w') : tau(w) - tau(w') in W_S^perp}, while within-subspace variance equals the sum of squared moduli of the folded harmonics C^{(W_S)}(delta_bar; x). Across the quotient cosets F_q^n / W_S, the Law of Total Variance partitions the non-zero Fourier difference spectrum into W_S^perp \\ {0} (between-coset variance) and F_q^n \\ W_S^perp (expected within-coset variance)."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Exact Projected Collision-Variety Pinching on W_S",
      "statement": "For any r-dimensional secret subspace W_S = colspan(G_S) in F_q^n, averaging P_(epsilon, sigma)(x | s) over s ~ Unif(W_S) pinches the double trajectory sum onto V_epsilon(f; W_S) = {(w, w') : tau_epsilon(w) - tau_epsilon(w') in W_S^perp} and equals sum_(delta in W_S^perp) C_(epsilon, sigma)(delta; x)."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Exact Folded Parseval Identity for Within-Subspace Secret Variance",
      "statement": "With folded harmonics C^(W_S)(delta_bar; x) = sum_(G_S^T delta == delta_bar mod q) C(delta; x), the within-subspace secret variance Var_(s ~ W_S)[P(x | s)] equals sum_(delta_bar in F_q^r \\ {0}) |C^(W_S)(delta_bar; x)|^2."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "Disjoint Harmonic Partition of Between-Coset and Within-Coset Variance Across F_q^n / W_S",
      "statement": "Across the q^(n-r) cosets W_S + a in F_q^n / W_S, the between-coset variance Var_a[E_(s ~ W_S+a)[P(x | s)]] equals sum_(delta in W_S^perp \\ {0}) |C(delta; x)|^2 and the expected within-coset variance E_a[Var_(s ~ W_S+a)[P(x | s)]] equals sum_(delta not in W_S^perp) |C(delta; x)|^2, summing to Var_(s ~ F_q^n)[P(x | s)]."
    }
  ],
  "title": "Native Higher-Call Secret-Subspace Restriction Audit: Projected Variety Pinching, Coset Harmonic Folding, and Fourier-Space Law of Total Variance"
